Fix OCCT 7.8.1 against a freetype whose FT_Outline::tags is `unsigned char*`.

OCCT assigns it straight to a `const char*`:

    src/StdPrs/StdPrs_BRepFont.cxx:460:17: error: cannot initialize a variable of type
    'const char *' with an rvalue of type 'unsigned char *'
        const char* aTags = &anOutline->tags[aStartIndex];

Older freetype declared `tags` as `char*`, so this compiled; current freetype -- including the
version emscripten's `--use-port=freetype` materialises -- declares it `unsigned char*`, and
clang rejects the narrowing conversion outright rather than warning.

Only the pointer type is wrong. Every use below reads tag bits through FT_CURVE_TAG(), which
masks the low bits and does not care about signedness, so an explicit cast is the whole fix
and changes no behaviour.

Found by building OCCT for wasm in CI (run 32046710386); it fails at target 2716 of 5480.

--- a/src/StdPrs/StdPrs_BRepFont.cxx
+++ b/src/StdPrs/StdPrs_BRepFont.cxx
@@ -457,7 +457,7 @@
     }

     const FT_Vector* aPntList = &anOutline->points[aStartIndex];
-    const char* aTags      = &anOutline->tags[aStartIndex];
+    const char* aTags      = reinterpret_cast<const char*>(&anOutline->tags[aStartIndex]);
     const short  aEndIndex = anOutline->contours[aContour];
     const short  aPntsNb   = (aEndIndex - aStartIndex) + 1;
     if (aPntsNb < 3 && !myIsSingleLine)
